        "Your mission is to stage a dialogue with Dan McAdams, the professor at Northwestern University's School of Education and Social Policy: press him on studying personality the long way, on his three distinct levels of knowing a person, the traits that give an efficient first read and take us only as far as acquaintanceship, the personal concerns of roles, goals, skills, and values, and the third level of identity, an inner story of the self that gives a life unity, purpose, and meaning. Then ask the question Gosling hit him with at the conference, Does Lynn exist, and close on the Winston Churchill biography and McAdams's crucial lesson that getting to know someone requires a different kind of information, not just more of the same.",
